From 56d3d733d1112310ed67c153a933635a994b77e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Resonate web port <dave.torosyan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:14:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Keep lyric lines that contain extender lines (melisma
 underscores)

OCR reads a lyric extender line ("pain____") as one wide word or as a
word glued to the syllable. Its width made OmrFont.computeSize report a
huge font, TextLine.checkValidity then rejected the WHOLE raw OCR line
before lyrics were built, and every syllable on that line was lost.

- TextWord: dash-only words (-, _, en/em dash) are recognized; the font
  of a word with a glued leading/trailing dash run is measured on its
  core characters only.
- TextLine: dash-only words are exempt from the font-size check; other
  too-big words (slur or tie pieces read as letters) are dropped from the
  line instead of the line itself, as long as at least 3 text words
  remain and at most 25% of the words are dropped.
- LyricItemInter: a one-char dash sitting on the baseline of the
  neighboring syllables is an extender (Extension), not a hyphen (mid
  x-height); a syllable followed by an extender is anchored a quarter of
  its width from its left side, since melisma syllables are left-aligned.

Measured on a 6-page pop vocal score: lyric syllables recognized 44% ->
87%, notes/pitch/rhythm unchanged; synthetic hymn/folk scores unchanged
or better.
